  "caption": "Instrumental original handheld JRPG underwater cue in F# minor, 4/4, 62 quarter-note BPM. Preserve the complete supplied 12-bar independent melody, varied phrase rests, explicit scene-specific support and bass. cello lead with organ support. Clean restrained timbres, no extra notes or reharmonization, no distortion, vocals or fade.",
  "form_description": "12 bars in slow 4/4: four-bar lonely cello cantilena with long rests; four-bar muted organ recollection; four-bar lower cello answer that ends before the loop. A deliberately sparse independent melody carries the deep sanctuary.",
  "reference_tracks": [
    80,
    82,
    91
  ],
  "composition_notes": "Independently authored literal tune, meter, form and groove for this region. Scalar passing notes retain their melodic shape while accompaniment thins to a consonant single tone or dyad; they are not forced into arpeggiated triads. A nearest-motion triadic anchor path guides harmonic direction. Independently selected bass avoids exposed parallel fifths/octaves, and scene-specific rests break its automatic doubling of the lead rhythm. Actual score and MIDI events are separately audited; this is not a claim of human listening approval.",
